          <figcaption class="lm__caveats">
            <p><strong>Caveat one.</strong> {THEM} adopting our dev techniques is easy because the pieces they need are the small ones: one instruction file, one CI job, a permission policy, a handoff habit. Our big pieces (pseudomonorepo rules, the skills library, the corpus) answer problems a single repo doesn't have, and they shouldn't adopt them.</p>
            <p><strong>Caveat two.</strong> Our learning from their product harness is real but not cheap. Replay and preflights are a few hundred lines each. A tiered synthetic-input harness is harder for memos than for exams: a "weak deal" is harder to fabricate convincingly than a weak candidate.</p>
