    <!-- 5 · Loops per layer ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="loops" id="ch-loops" aria-labelledby="s2s-loops">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">ch · the loops</p>
        <h2 id="s2s-loops">The loops, per layer</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">Same four lanes in every diagram. The two layers cross in one place: on {THEM}'s side, a finding from the in-product loop often becomes a platform change in the developer loop.</p>

        <h3 class="loops__h">Developer loops</h3>
        <div class="loop-notes">
          <p><strong>{THEM}.</strong> A design doc is signed off first, but the session starts cold: there is no instruction file. The agent implements, checks with the <code>verify</code> skill, node tests and an ad-hoc browser drive, and commits with a measured message. Memory is the git log, and sometimes a "what shipped" section.</p>
          <p><strong>Lossless.</strong> A signed-off spec, a plan per phase re-grounded on the code, an agent loaded with layered instructions and skills, then a proof ladder. A red proof stops it. A green one leads to a changelog entry, a commit with CI, a handoff, and a corpus the next session queries.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="s2s-figure">
          <figcaption class="s2s-figure__title">{THEM} · developer loop</figcaption>
          <div class="s2s-figure__svg s2s-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${THEM}'s developer loop, scrollable`} set:html={loopDevThemSvg} />
        </figure>
        <figure class="s2s-figure">
          <figcaption class="s2s-figure__title">Lossless · developer loop</figcaption>
          <div class="s2s-figure__svg s2s-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="The Lossless developer loop, scrollable" set:html={loopDevOursSvg} />
        </figure>

        <h3 class="loops__h">In-product loops</h3>
        <div class="loop-notes">
          <p><strong>{THEM}: generating an exam.</strong> Source text and notes go to an agent that reads the rulebook and the craft ledger. <code>/exam-build</code>, or its in-product twin <code>/studio</code>, drafts a sketch and stops for sign-off. The exam is assembled from a skeleton and validated, then run through simulated candidates with error bars and preflights. Every change must name the defect it fixes; findings go to the ledger. Then a human sits the exam.</p>
          <p><strong>Lossless: generating a memo.</strong> Deal inputs, an outline YAML and runtime rules, section writers working from a closed corpus, then citation and fact-checking agents. The memo is evaluated and scored once. An analyst revises or exports, and lessons land in issue-resolution files or an <code>AGENTS.md</code> rule. Replay, tiered inputs and error bars are the missing step.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="s2s-figure">
          <figcaption class="s2s-figure__title">{THEM} · in-product loop</figcaption>
          <div class="s2s-figure__svg s2s-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${THEM}'s in-product loop, scrollable`} set:html={loopProductThemSvg} />
        </figure>
